Upstream package
----------------
PearsonDS 1.3.2, "Pearson Distribution System"
Date: 2025-03-24
Authors: Martin Becker, Stefan Kloessner
Contributor: Joel Heinrich
Upstream license declaration: GPL (>= 2)

This repository is a modern Fortran translation of the computational portions
of that package. Plotting code (R/plots.r), package loading/registration glue,
and R-specific user-interface code are intentionally omitted.

Pearson type IV attribution
---------------------------
The upstream src/pearsonIV.c states that its code is partially adapted from:

  CDF/MEMO/STATISTICS/PUBLIC/6820
  "A Guide to the Pearson Type IV Distribution"
  Joel Heinrich, University of Pennsylvania, December 21, 2004

The Fortran type-IV normalization and rejection sampler retain that provenance.

r_mod.f90
---------
The user supplied r_mod.f90 for reuse and identified it as MIT-licensed. Its
implementation is reused directly; only formatting-only line wrapping and an
SPDX/provenance header were added so that standard free-form Fortran compilers
accept its long lines. No copyright-holder information was present in the
supplied source, so none was invented.
